{title: 192 - O Shepherd Divine}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #192 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 192}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]O Shepherd divine, I know Thou art mine; Thy [Bb7]search in the night was for [Eb]me.
[Eb]This bleak world is cold, but warm is Thy fold; My [Bb7]Shepherd, I follow [Eb]Thee.
[Eb]Thy [Ab]beautiful lamp shineth [Eb]bright o'er my way,
[Eb]Thy [F7]glorious light unto [Bb]Thy per[F7]fect [Bb7]day.
[Eb]Thro' pastures serene, Thro' valleys of green, My [Bb7]Shepherd, I follow [Eb]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Eb]O Shepherd [Bb7]divine, I know [Eb]Thou art mine;
[Eb]Thy great [Bb7]heart was [Eb]broken for me.
[Eb]Thy grace and [Ab]Thy law I [Eb]picture in awe;
[Eb][F7]They [Bb]kissed [F7]upon [Bb7]Calvary.
[Eb]Ah! life that [Bb7]was given to [Eb]ransom my soul,
[Eb]Ah! heart that [Bb7]was broken to [Eb]make sinners whole,
[Eb]This world is [Bb7]but loss In [Eb]view of Thy cross,
[Eb]My [Ab]Shepherd, I [Eb]follow Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Eb]O Shepherd [Bb7]divine, I know [Eb]Thou art mine;
[Eb]I hear [Bb7]Thee say, [Eb]"Follow thou Me."
[Eb]Thy message [Ab]today illumines [Eb]my way;
[Eb][F7]The [Bb]Spirit [F7]of [Bb7]Prophecy.
[Eb]I thrill at [Bb7]Thy marvelous love [Eb]to Thy sheep,
[Eb]The way Thou [Bb7]dost lead to [Eb]the still waters deep,
[Eb]One staff and [Bb7]one rod, One [Eb]fold and one God,
[Eb]My [Ab]Shepherd, I [Eb]follow Thee.
{end_of_verse}
